 "_about": "Clamp-slip glide per-note scaling, UNIFORM-FRICTION MODEL (a hypothesis, not a derived certainty): df/f = -(l_c/(2 mu N)) * K' * A, K' = omega^4 Q^3 / (M1 E I_root t_c), from a Rayleigh treatment of a root compliance (general for taper and solder), with the slip zone shed linearly under uniform clamp pressure (kappa = 1/2 exactly). Same finite-element reed blanks as the swing prior. K_finger refers to swing at the pickup finger region. Supplied by the physics review, 2026-09-27; supersedes the first (-2 dL/L) export. Uniform friction over-predicts the shift by 10-100x for plausible clamp loads, so the real clamp carries the moment mainly by bearing with slip a corner residual: the per-note scaling and the exponent (slip ~ M^n, n in [1, 2]) are not derivable without clamp geometry. Above MIDI 72 the blank geometry does not reach pitch.",
